llama.cpp: llama.cpp is an open-source C/C++ library designed to run large
llama.cpp: language models (LLMs) efficiently with minimal setup. Its main goal
llama.cpp: is to enable high-performance LLM inference across a wide range of
llama.cpp: hardware, both locally and in the cloud. It has no external
llama.cpp: dependencies and supports various architectures including Apple
llama.cpp: silicon, x86, and RISC-V, along with GPU backends like CUDA, AMD HIP,
llama.cpp: Vulkan, and SYCL. A key feature is integer quantization (from 1.5-bit
llama.cpp: to 8-bit), which reduces memory usage and speeds up inference, and it
llama.cpp: also allows CPU+GPU hybrid processing for models not fitting in VRAM.
